%
% TWO LEVELS OF "VERIFIED", AND THEY ARE NOT THE SAME THING:
%
%   metadata verified - the volume, pages, year and DOI below were checked
%     against Crossref (api.crossref.org) or the publisher's own page, not
%     written from memory. Every DOI resolves.
%
%   source read - somebody on the team has actually opened the paper and can
%     say what it argues. This is what the Literature Review needs, and it is
%     what an examiner probes. Metadata being right does not make a citation
%     honest if nobody read the thing.
%
% Each entry records both. Do not cite an entry whose "read by" line is still
% empty: either read it, or drop it from the bibliography.
%
% BibTeX note: '%' comments must sit OUTSIDE the braces. A comment placed after
% the last field inside an entry makes BibTeX skip the whole entry silently -
% which is how all six of these were broken until the report was first compiled.

